   {
    "flag": "--kv-bits",
    "arg": "B",
    "takes_value": true,
    "type": "float",
    "hint": "is the JOINT K/V ceiling (one number for the whole stack); --kv-k-bits with --kv-v-bits is the SPLIT form, where each plane's per-layer layering is solved in its own budget and a layer whose K and V requirements meet no single tier is refused by index with the missing (K,V) cell named. --kv-bits-mode split (default) | joint | ceiling picks the reading. Both planes always cost the same bits per element: one DType drives both."
   },
